🚽 Test case: round-12 review finding #5 -- infer_expression_type()'s
🚽 static NODE_STRUCT_ACCESS fallback previously only resolved a DIRECT
🚽 identifier object (`f.c`), via a single linear scan of the object's own
🚽 struct fields. A chained access like `o.inner.v` has an object that is
🚽 itself a NODE_STRUCT_ACCESS, not a NODE_IDENTIFIER, so it fell straight
🚽 through to NONE -- silently disabling argument type-checking for this
🚽 shape (semantic_check_native_call()'s `actual == NONE` fallthrough),
🚽 exactly the class of hole this whole typed-ABI phase exists to close.
🚽 infer_struct_def_static() now resolves a chain of any depth purely off
🚽 the analyzer's own symbol table + struct-definition registry (never
🚽 runtime storage), so this must now be caught statically, the same as
🚽 the single-level case already was.
gang Inner {
